<spell-notebook "rating theming">
	<header level="1">
		Rating
		<header>A rating indicates user interest in content.</>
	</>
	<rating-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-rating-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (`:root` included), or on
			the group's box through `::part(rating)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each through a
			private alias, so nothing inside blocks them. Style one icon with `::part(icon)`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* every rating on the page */
			:root {
			  --ui-rating-icon-width: 1.5em;
			}
			/* one kind:  quieter empty icons */
			ui-rating.reviews {
			  --ui-rating-inactive-color: var(--ui-border-color);
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				`color` sets the filled icons' hue through the shared colour remap (`--ui-color`), so a coloured rating ignores
				`--ui-rating-active-color` (filled) and `--ui-rating-selected-color` (the hover preview); `size` scales the
				whole rating. Never set the `--_ui-*` names: they're the
				sheet's private plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-rating" playground>
				<ui-rating value="3" aria-label="Rating"></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu in the header (Spell, Glass, Fruity, Merlot, Paper, Midnight, Crisp, Pop, Matrix) changes the colours and fonts a rating
			inherits.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
